              "type": "heading",
              "tag": "h2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "CLAIMED: the 6 arithmetic operators the sealed formulas use split by what they do over the corpus's own integers — 2 commutative (* +), 3 forced on their diagonal (% - /), 1 neither (^) — and 2 + 3 + 1 = 6."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "lean",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "((2 + 3 + 1 = 6) ∧ (3 > 2)) ∧ (2 > 1)"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "lean",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "theorem the_arithmetic_alphabet_partitions_by_its_own_algebra : ((2 + 3 + 1 = 6) ∧ (3 > 2)) ∧ (2 > 1) := by decide"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page",
          "slug": "theorem-most_of_the_unstated_remainder_stays_inside_one_wing",
